     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\">Hello all,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\"><br></span></p><p style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\">We have a funded (UK/EU) PhD\r\nopportunity at the Diabetes Research Centre, University of Leicester, for a\r\nstudent to use accelerometer data to look at physical activity/movement\r\npatterns indicative of pre-frailty and frailty. The project would suit an\r\nenthusiastic student with a background in Data Science and a strong interest in\r\nhealth and lifestyle. <u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\"><br></span></p><p style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\">The student would gain skills\r\nin accelerometry, signal processing, statistics, and epidemiology. The project\r\nbenefits from a multi-disciplinary collaboration between researchers with\r\nexpertise in lifestyle, accelerometery, engineering and frailty. <u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\"><br></span></p><p style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm\">Details available at either of\r\nthe links below:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:105%\"><a href=\"https://www.findaphd.com/phds/project/identification-of-movement-patterns-indicative-of-frailty-and-pre-frailty-using-wearable-activity-monitors/?p107915\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.findaphd.com/phds/project/identification-of-movement-patterns-indicative-of-frailty-and-pre-frailty-using-wearable-activity-monitors/?p107915&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792491263588000&amp;usg=AOvVaw29TnW08NNXOxmUV1XLAk8G\">Find a PhD - accelerometer and frailty</a><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:105%\"><a href=\"https://www2.le.ac.uk/research-degrees/funding/life-sciences\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www2.le.ac.uk/research-degrees/funding/life-sciences&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792491263588000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hx_4PpmdDRLDIyhNJd_Z5\">Leicester PhD - accelerometer and frailty</a></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Please\r\nfeel free to contact me if you have any queries or would like any further\r\ninformation (<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">alex.r...@leicester.ac.uk</a>),<u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:105%\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Alex\r\nRowlands<u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:105%\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:105%\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<br></div>"
